# Claude folder-trust pre-seed rules
# Scopes the core source that pre-seeds ~/.claude.json folder-trust at worktree
# creation (the claudetrust leaf package + its call site in Prepare) plus the
# daemon-delegated fallback path (used when Prepare runs inside the OS sandbox
# and the ~/.claude.json write is denied: the daemon performs the privileged
# write, deriving trusted paths from the worktree registry) and the E2E
# scenarios that assert the seeded trust keys. Changes to these should trigger
# the trust scenarios, which drive a real `plan init --worktree` and verify the
# per-path trust keys land in the sandbox ~/.claude.json. Paths are relative to
# the flow repo root.

../core/pkg/claudetrust/seeder.go
../core/pkg/workspace/prepare.go
../core/pkg/workspace/types.go
../core/util/pathutil/normalize.go
# Daemon-delegated trust seeding (privileged fallback for sandboxed callers).
../core/pkg/daemon/client.go
../core/pkg/daemon/remote.go
../core/pkg/daemon/local.go
../daemon/internal/daemon/server/trust_handler.go
# flow wiring: the injected fallback closure + the add-worktrees direct path.
pkg/orchestration/trust_seeder.go
cmd/plan_add_worktrees.go
tests/e2e/tend/scenarios/coordinator_workflow.go
tests/e2e/tend/scenarios/claude_trust_seed.go
